# Bytes Encoding Fix for anypb.Any Type

This PR fixes an issue where bytes encoding settings were not being respected in nested `anypb.Any` fields in the Substreams CLI.

## Problem

In Substreams CLI, we render Protobuf to JSON using the upcoming Golang JSON V2 module. We define how we want bytes to be encoded correctly, which works well for top-level messages. However, when a message has a field of type `anypb.Any`, the inner JSON object rendered does not respect our bytes encoding settings.

## Solution

The fix is implemented in our fork of the `jhump/protoreflect` library. We modified the `anyResolver.Resolve` method in `dynamic/json.go` to ensure that when a message contains an `anypb.Any` field, the inner JSON object rendered will respect the same bytes encoding configuration that is set for the top-level message.

This ensures consistent bytes encoding throughout the entire JSON output, providing a better user experience.

## Testing

The fix has been verified with a test case that confirms bytes encoding settings are properly propagated to nested `anypb.Any` fields.

